From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 23:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a refused click says so

The desktop on a tty draws a pointer and the trackpad moves it, and
clicking does nothing -- on the pad and on a USB mouse both. Those take
different routes into the browser (`BTN_LEFT` through
`EventConverterEvdevImpl`, the pad's through libinput), so a fault that
takes both is downstream of both, and the next question is simply
whether a click reaches the window at all.

THE LOG THAT WAS SUPPOSED TO ANSWER THAT CANNOT. Patch 0025 logs `the
first pointer event reached the window` once, gated on
`event->IsLocatedEvent()`. `SetFullscreen` -> `SetBoundsInPixels` ->
`SendBoundsChange` -> `DrmCursor::CommitBoundsChange` ->
`DrmWindowHost::SynthesizeMouseMove` -> `EventFactoryEvdev::
SynthesizeMouseMove` posts a `kMouseMoved` carrying `EF_IS_SYNTHESIZED`
(`ui/events/ozone/evdev/event_factory_evdev.cc:583`) on every startup,
and it is posted from inside `CommitBoundsChange` -- the one instant when
the cursor's rect and `bounds_` are equal by construction, so it always
passes the bounds test. In the log from the machine it fired 222ms in, a
full second before the first key:

  155032.990310  domicile: the first pointer event reached the window
  155034.050269  domicile: the first key event reached the window

Nobody had touched anything. Patch 0026's message read that ordering as
proof the trackpad worked -- "the trackpad works and always did" -- and
it was proof of nothing. A one-shot a synthesized event always spends is
not a diagnostic, it is a trap, and it caught its own author twice.

So three things this window can now say, and between them they separate
the candidates in one run:

A REFUSED POINTER EVENT. `CanDispatchEvent`'s located branch is
`return bounds_.Contains(located_event->location())`
(`drm_window_host.cc:397-399`) with no log on the way out, and the
function's own `TODO(spang): For non-ash builds we would need smarter
keyboard focus.` three lines later says whose policy it is. A click
dropped there and a click never read off the device look identical from
outside the process and want opposite fixes. Now it says so once, with
the location AND the bounds, because a window whose rect and whose
cursor have drifted apart is the interesting case and the difference
between those two numbers is the whole answer.

THE FIRST PRESS, ASKED ABOUT SEPARATELY from motion, because they fail
separately: motion can reach the page while a press is swallowed by a
non-client hit test. And the cursor being drawn says nothing about
either -- that is the cursor plane, moved from the evdev thread by
`DrmCursor`, which never reaches a renderer.

WHAT VIEWS ANSWERED. `DispatchEventFromNativeUiEvent` returns the
`EventResult` and this call discarded it (`:243-245` at the pin), so a
press that arrived and a press that arrived and was wanted by nothing
were the same observation. `ER_UNHANDLED` on the first press means the
event got to the widget and no view claimed it, which is a different bug
from never arriving and has a different fix.

The existing pointer line keeps its name but not its meaning: it now
fires for the first located event NOT carrying `EF_IS_SYNTHESIZED`, so
it answers the question it was always supposed to.

No behavior changes. Every addition is a VLOG(1) and a bool, and the
one non-logging edit -- reading `DispatchEventFromNativeUiEvent`'s return
value instead of dropping it -- does not alter what is dispatched or what
this returns.
---
 ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.cc | 54 +++++++++++++++++--
 ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.h  |  2 +
 2 files changed, 53 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.cc b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.cc
index f0f0412801..5227fd20b0 100644
--- a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.cc
+++ b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.cc
@@ -396,7 +396,19 @@ bool DrmWindowHost::CanDispatchEvent(const PlatformEvent& event) {
     return display_bounds == bounds_;
   } else if (event->IsLocatedEvent()) {
     LocatedEvent* located_event = event->AsLocatedEvent();
-    return bounds_.Contains(located_event->location());
+    const bool inside = bounds_.Contains(located_event->location());
+    // A LOCATED EVENT REFUSED HERE IS REFUSED IN SILENCE, and that silence is
+    // indistinguishable from one that was never read off a device at all.
+    // Both look like a desktop that ignores the mouse, and they want opposite
+    // fixes. Said once, with both numbers, because the interesting case is a
+    // window whose bounds and whose cursor have drifted apart -- and if they
+    // have, the difference is the whole diagnosis.
+    if (!inside && !std::exchange(said_a_pointer_was_refused_, true)) {
+      VLOG(1) << "domicile: a pointer event at "
+              << located_event->location().ToString() << " is outside this "
+              << "window's " << bounds_.ToString() << ", so it was refused";
+    }
+    return inside;
   }
 
   // TODO(spang): For non-ash builds we would need smarter keyboard focus.
@@ -419,8 +431,34 @@ uint32_t DrmWindowHost::DispatchEvent(const PlatformEvent& event) {
   if (event->IsKeyEvent() && !std::exchange(said_a_key_arrived_, true)) {
     VLOG(1) << "domicile: the first key event reached the window";
   } else if (event->IsLocatedEvent() &&
+             !(event->flags() & EF_IS_SYNTHESIZED) &&
              !std::exchange(said_a_pointer_arrived_, true)) {
-    VLOG(1) << "domicile: the first pointer event reached the window";
+    VLOG(1) << "domicile: the first pointer event a hand caused reached the "
+            << "window";
+  }
+
+  // NOT `IsLocatedEvent()` ALONE, WHICH IS WHAT THIS USED TO BE, AND IT COST A
+  // WRONG DIAGNOSIS. `SetFullscreen` -> `SetBoundsInPixels` ->
+  // `SendBoundsChange` -> `DrmCursor::CommitBoundsChange` ->
+  // `SynthesizeMouseMove` posts a `kMouseMoved` carrying `EF_IS_SYNTHESIZED`
+  // (`ui/events/ozone/evdev/event_factory_evdev.cc:583`) about 200ms into
+  // every startup -- and at the one instant when the cursor's rect and
+  // `bounds_` are equal by construction, so it always passes the test above.
+  // A one-shot gated only on `IsLocatedEvent()` is therefore spent before
+  // anybody has touched anything, and patch 0026's message read its presence
+  // as proof the trackpad worked. It was not proof of anything.
+  //
+  // A PRESS IS ASKED ABOUT SEPARATELY because motion and buttons fail
+  // separately: motion can reach the page while a press is swallowed by a
+  // non-client hit test, and the cursor being drawn says nothing about either
+  // -- that is the cursor plane, driven from the evdev thread, which never
+  // reaches the renderer.
+  const bool first_press = event->type() == EventType::kMousePressed &&
+                           !std::exchange(said_a_press_arrived_, true);
+  if (first_press) {
+    VLOG(1) << "domicile: the first mouse press reached the window at "
+            << event->AsLocatedEvent()->location().ToString()
+            << ", in a window at " << bounds_.ToString();
   }
 
   if (event->IsLocatedEvent()) {
@@ -439,9 +477,19 @@ uint32_t DrmWindowHost::DispatchEvent(const PlatformEvent& event) {
     located_event->set_location_f(location);
     located_event->set_root_location_f(location);
   }
-  DispatchEventFromNativeUiEvent(
+  // THE ANSWER WAS ALWAYS HERE AND NOBODY READ IT. This returns the
+  // `EventResult` views came back with, and the call discarded it, so a click
+  // that arrived and a click that arrived and was wanted by nothing looked
+  // identical from outside the process. `ER_UNHANDLED` on the first press
+  // means the event got all the way to the widget and no view claimed it,
+  // which is a different bug from never arriving.
+  const EventResult result = DispatchEventFromNativeUiEvent(
       event, base::BindOnce(&PlatformWindowDelegate::DispatchEvent,
                             base::Unretained(delegate_)));
+  if (first_press) {
+    VLOG(1) << "domicile: views answered the first mouse press with "
+            << (result == ER_HANDLED ? "ER_HANDLED" : "ER_UNHANDLED");
+  }
   return POST_DISPATCH_STOP_PROPAGATION;
 }
 
diff --git a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.h b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.h
index a0d9a09cf6..b29db82526 100644
--- a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.h
+++ b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/host/drm_window_host.h
@@ -142,6 +142,8 @@ class DrmWindowHost : public PlatformWindow,
   // everything under this line is silent when it works.
   bool said_a_key_arrived_ = false;
   bool said_a_pointer_arrived_ = false;
+  bool said_a_press_arrived_ = false;
+  bool said_a_pointer_was_refused_ = false;
   std::optional<gfx::Rect> restored_bounds_;
   // What this window last told views it is. Upstream answers kUnknown forever,
   // which makes DesktopWindowTreeHostPlatform::IsFullscreen() permanently
